why:
Self-service yards crush cars 30-90 days after they are set. D-626 says nothing is bought before the design freeze (DS11), which is weeks of CAD and calculation away. By then today's donors are gone. Today's search (sightings SG17-SG32) found:
- one aluminum 5.3 without AFM in all of the Front Range: an LM4 in a 2004 Envoy XL at Colorado Springs, set 21 days ago;
- eleven AFM 5.3s (LC9, LH6), which keep arriving;
- four V8 AWD Explorers and Mountaineers with the solid 8.8;
- no 350Z, and one G35 coupe whose gearbox is unknown.

A donor in hand also makes the CAD exact (R11: a measured part beats a model). The engine family (D-393) and the axle (D-623) are already ruled, and every FB V8 build found fits an LS.
